.SH PLUGINS
.sp
Ziro Shell organizes plugins into three distinct execution stages for optimal shell performance:
.TP
.B \fBEager Tools (Stage 2/4)\fP
Loaded synchronously during bootstrap before the prompt renders. Includes completion engines (\fBzsh\-completions\fP, \fBcompinit\fP), prompt infrastructure (\fBstarship\fP), and terminal keybindings.
.TP
.B \fBDeferred Plugins (Stage 5)\fP
Loaded non-blockingly during shell idle cycles via \fBziro\-defer\fP. Includes syntax highlighting (\fBfast\-syntax\-highlighting\fP), autocomplete (\fBziro\-ghost\fP, \fBzsh\-autosuggestions\fP), and menu enhancement (\fBfzf\-tab\fP).
.TP
.B \fBOn-Demand Proxies (Stage 7)\fP
Loaded strictly on first invocation through transparent function stubs. Includes \fBzoxide\fP (triggered by \fBz\fP, \fBzi\fP), fuzzy finder (\fBfzf\fP via \fB^R\fP), and directory tagging (\fBwd\fP).
.sp
Run \fBziro plugin list\fP to view the active status, load stage, and description of all registered plugins.
